<description>
Summarize a gridded table of colored square sprites as count bars ordered by increasing count.

Input structure
The input is a table on a dominant background. A unique non-background color
forms full horizontal and vertical gridline bars. Each occupied table cell
contains one solid 2 by 2 square sprite, and some sprites may use the same
color as the gridline.

Rule
Ignore empty cells and ignore sprites whose color is the gridline color. For
every other sprite color, count how many table cells contain that color.
Create one output row per counted color, sorted by increasing count; each row
is a left-aligned horizontal bar of that color with length equal to its
count, padded with background to the maximum count.

Key insight
The large grid is only a frequency table: the separator color is not part of
the histogram, even when it appears as a cell sprite.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "table-cell 2 by 2 sprites s whose color differs from the unique full-row/full-column gridline color, grouped by color",
  "dst": "output rows d ordered top-to-bottom by increasing sprite count",
  "match_cond": "rank(s.sprite_count ascending) == rank(d top-to-bottom); counts are unique",
  "transform": "fill the leftmost s.sprite_count cells of d with s.color and leave the remaining cells background",
  "grid_shape": "height is number of counted colors; width is largest counted sprite count"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  background: 0
  grid:
    separator_bars: 3 row bars always at rows 4,9,14; 2-4 column bars at cols 4,9,14,19 (spacing 5)
    cell_structure: bars divide grid into 4 row-spans x 3-5 col-spans; first spans are 4-wide, trailing span may be a 1-3 wide stub
    grid_size: height 16 or 19; width 13-21; determined by bar count + trailing stub
  separator_color: one unique non-bg color forming all full-row and full-column bars
  cells:
    usable: cells with height>=3 AND width>=3 (stubs <=2 wide are always empty)
    sprites: each usable cell contains exactly one solid 2x2 square at local position (1,1); no usable cell is empty [observed]
    colors: 3-5 distinct non-bg sprite colors including separator color
    separator_sprites: some usable cells use the separator color as sprite; these are excluded from counting
    counted_colors: 2-4 distinct non-separator sprite colors with unique counts each
  output:
    rows: one per counted color, sorted ascending by count
    width: max count; each row is left-aligned bar of that color padded with bg
generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose N_colors (2-4) counted colors and separator color, all distinct, none 0
    2. Assign unique counts c_1 < c_2 < ... < c_N to counted colors; max count = c_N (range 2-4)
    3. Build output grid (N_colors rows x c_N cols) with left-aligned color bars
    4. Compute usable_cells = sum of all counts + number of separator-colored sprites; choose table_rows=3-4 usable row spans, table_cols=2-4 usable col spans such that table_rows*table_cols >= sum(counts) + sep_sprites
    5. Fill usable cells randomly with the counted-color sprites (exact counts) plus separator-color sprites to fill remaining cells
    6. Build input grid: 3 row bars at 4,9,14; col bars at 4,9,...; optionally add a trailing stub (1-3 cells) after last bar in rows and/or cols; place 2x2 sprites at (1,1) in each usable cell; fill bar rows/cols with separator color
